 "storage": "⛔ The assembled bowl does not keep — the dill is finished within twenty minutes of leaving the pan and there is no reviving it. Marinated raw fish keeps 1 day covered in the fridge, and a few hours in the turmeric does more for it than twenty minutes ever will. Cooked fish keeps 2 days but reheat it in a pan rather than a microwave, and add fresh dill at the end rather than trying to rescue yesterday's. Nước chấm keeps a week.",
 "chefNotes": "⚖️ Buy the dill by weight, not by habit. A supermarket sprig-pack is roughly 20g and this dish wants more of it per person than most people use in a month.\n\n✅ Hot pan, then leave the fish alone. It tells you when it is ready by letting go of the pan, and no amount of poking makes that happen sooner.\n\n⚠️ Galangal and ginger are not interchangeable here even though they look alike. Galangal is sharper, more pine-like and much more fibrous — grate it fine or you will be picking threads out of the pan.\n\n⛔ Do not skip the shrimp paste to make it milder. Five grams is not a flavour, it is an amplifier, and the dish without it is the same dish with the volume turned down.",
