   "trivia": "The chay kitchens of Huế make this constantly, and the mung bean is not standing in for the shrimp so much as replacing what the shrimp was for. ⚖️ Dried shrimp brought salt, savour and a dry fibrous texture in one ingredient; steamed mung bean, mashed and then dried out in a pan, gives the texture and a mild earthiness but none of the salt, so the nước chấm has to carry more of it. ⚠️ Push the soy and the lime up together rather than the soy alone, or the sauce goes flat and dark instead of sharp.",
