 "storage": "Holds 3 days chilled and is better on the second day than the first, because the tofu carries on taking up sauce for hours after the pan comes off. ⚠️ Reheat it gently and without stirring — the slabs are softer once they have been chilled and they break far more readily than they did in the pan. ⛔ Freezing changes it permanently: tofu forms ice crystals that tear the curd into a spongy, chewy texture. Some people like that a great deal, but it is not this dish any more.",
 "chefNotes": "⚖️ Press it, then weigh it. A block that has not lost weight has no room in it, and everything else on this card depends on the room.\n\n✅ Cool the fried tofu before it goes in the sauce. Five minutes on a rack, and it will drink the pan instead of wearing it.\n\n⚠️ Keep the sauce loose. Anything that has reduced to a cling is a sauce that can no longer be absorbed by anything.\n\n⛔ Stop stirring the moment the tofu goes in. The fried skin is the only thing holding each slab together and a spoon will find that out for you.",
